---
name: "TypeScript Best Practices"
description: "Coding standards and practices for TypeScript development"
alwaysApply: true
---

When working with TypeScript code, please follow these guidelines:

- Use strict TypeScript configuration
- Always define explicit types for function parameters and return values
- Use interfaces for object types instead of type aliases when possible
- Prefer readonly properties when data shouldn't be mutated
- Use union types instead of enums when appropriate
- Always handle null and undefined cases
- Use generic types to make code reusable
- Document public APIs with TSDoc comments
